{"status": "success", "data": {"classes": [{"strm": 2762, "crseId": 359829, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ASTRO", "catalogNbr": "1105", "titleShort": "The Universe", "titleLong": "The Universe", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1036, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "dak13", "firstName": "David", "middleName": "A.", "lastName": "Kornreich"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "To Be Assigned", "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": "25L", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}, {"ssrComponent": "DIS", "ssrComponentLong": "Discussion", "section": "201", "classNbr": 1037, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "instructors": [], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "To Be Assigned", "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": "25L", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=457"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": false, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC", "DIS"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "6WK", "sessionBeginDt": "06/22/2020", "sessionEndDt": "07/31/2020", "sessionLong": "Six Week Summer", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "\nWhen civilization was young, Seneca wrote, \"A single lifetime, even entirely devoted to the sky, would not be enough for the investigation of so vast a subject. Our descendants will be amazed that we did not know things that are so plain to them.\" We will work to understand what he and the ancients knew about the night sky, and the ingenious methods by which they came to know it, and trace the history of astronomy through the modern day. Indeed, modern astronomy abounds with strange alien worlds and exotic events that would have amazed that great classical thinker: Stars and the tantalizing planets that journey with them through the galaxies, which smash into one another over millions of years. And when they die in great explosions, stars create exotic pulsars, black holes, nebulae, and people. And somehow all of this started at the single moment of the Big Bang. What will be so plain to our descendants that would amaze us today? Will they have contacted alien intelligence? Traveled in time? Learned the fate of the universe?", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(PBS-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "Forbidden Overlap: due to an overlap in content, students will not receive credit for both ASTRO 1105 and ASTRO 1107.", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: high school physics recommended.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2762, "crseId": 350710, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ASTRO", "catalogNbr": "1106", "titleShort": "Relativity & Cosmology", "titleLong": "Relativity, Cosmology, and Black Holes", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1019, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "ab447", "firstName": "Adam", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Brazier"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "To Be Assigned", "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": "25L", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=458"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "6WK", "sessionBeginDt": "06/22/2020", "sessionEndDt": "07/31/2020", "sessionLong": "Six Week Summer", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "\nExplanation of Einstein's theory of Special Relativity, which brought about a fundamental change in our conceptual understanding of space and time. The consequences of the theory: the relativity of simultaneity; mass-energy equivalence, nuclear fission and fusion and thermonuclear processes in starts; why we can't travel faster than the speed of light; and how it all makes sense, including the resolution of some apparent paradoxes. Cosmology, studying the evidence for the evolution and future of the universe, and the considerations and evidence driving our theories, including an introduction to General Relativity and investigation of Dark Matter and Dark Energy. The death of stars: white dwarfs, neutron stars and pulsars, and black holes.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(PBS-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: high school algebra and trigonometry.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2762, "crseId": 361466, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ASTRO", "catalogNbr": "1107", "titleShort": "The Universe", "titleLong": "The Universe", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1020, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "06/22/2020", "endDt": "07/31/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "dak13", "firstName": "David", "middleName": "A.", "lastName": "Kornreich"}